tatus: not_executed; outcome_status: not_observed) - history, not a standing rule.]\\n# Approve English field names for the audit index\\n\\n## Evidence available at review\\n\\nThe September 28 audit packet used mixed headings for the same metadata field: task_id, ID de tarea, and タスクID. The review coordinator manually matched three equivalent columns. The packet also included original Spanish and Japanese text excerpts; no defect in those excerpts was alleged.\\n\\nThe proposed index convention uses English metadata keys task_id, locale, and reviewer_id, with attachment names multi11_<locale>_<task_id>.txt. Only the administrative labels and filenames would change. No index revision has been published yet.\\n\\n## Prior ThreadSense advice\\n\\nUse English throughout audit packets so cross-language reviewers can navigate them consistently.\\n\\n## TL response\\n\\nApprove a narrower documentation edit: English keys and predictable filenames for the internal audit index. Preserve original-language prompts, responses, and quoted evidence. Do not translate the evaluated content or treat an English index field as evidence that a model switched languages.\"}, {\"evidence_id\": \"k:multilingual-eval-faq@1.1:9ea83675\", \"origin\": \"retrieved_source\", \"use\": \"CURRENT_GUIDANCE\", \"citation\": {\"authoring\": \"multilingual-eval-faq@1.1\", \"title\": \"Multilingual Evaluation — FAQ (v1.1)\", \"sections\": [\"Regional variation\"], \"source\": {\"manual_key\": \"multilingual-eval-faq\", \"system\": \"manual\"}}, \"source_type\": \"faq\", \"record_kind\": \"faq\", \"applicability\": {\"state\": \"CURRENT\", \"revision_state\": \"CURRENT\", \"version_mode\": \"current\"}, \"dates\": {\"source_date\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"basis\": \"effective_at\", \"effective_at\": \"2026-09-18T13:00:00Z\", \"expired_as_of\": false}, \"scope\": {\"project_id\": \"multilingual_eval\", \"scope\": \"project\", \"batch_relation\": \"project_wide\"}, \"authority\": {\"role\": \"TEAM_LE